\f2\fs22 \'93Well, what in the name of The Dawkins have we here? Eight prime examples of the Elvi.\'94 Kleo was startled by the sudden visit by so many Elvi. 
\f3\i What could they want?
\f2\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, great Sages. We have been sent to by the High Elvis on business most urgent. The Dawkins be praised.\'94 Karate Elvis was in charge.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You know of the Dawkins?\'94 He was immensely surprised that these clones not only had knowledge of The Dawkins, but appeared to revere the great one.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, we were awoken to his words by the great Teacher. He appeared before us and told of The Dawkins, Darwin and the beauty of science and reason. He told us of the one-after-the-one and of the Blessed Mother. We study the Chronicles of the Dawkins, we study science and sing in the name of the one to come.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is indeed gratifying that the word of The Dawkins has spread to the Elvi.\'94 Kleoboulos said. 
\f3\i Why didn\'92t I think of that? 
\f2\i0 \'93I will have to meet this great teacher. Who is this Blessed Mother you speak of?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is rumoured she is with child and carries the one-after-the-one. There is great joy throughout the entire Elvi.\'94 Karate glanced to either side and was gratified to see his brethren were nodding in agreement.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Excellent, excellent.\'94 Kleo looked towards his two colleagues who both imperceptibly nodded and grinned. \'91Now, what is this urgent business you have been sent here to discuss.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Five of our number have succumbed to the infection of religion and the promise of certainty.\'94 Wing Chun offered up.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Certainty? The most delusional state of mind. Which sect?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They are possessed by the Jesus.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93This is very serious, but I think I might be able to help. What manner of delivery system?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Gospel music.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Mmm, yes.\'94 He said gravely \'93I can see why the Elvi might find Gospel attractive. Solo, Chilo, come we have much work to do. The longer we wait, the further we will have to walk.\'94 Kleo headed to exit.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Elvis, Elvis and Elvis will stay here and guard your keep, while Elvis, Elvis, Elvis, Elvis and I will escort you to the Quarter.\'94 Said Elvis.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Maybe you should think about getting different names.\'94 Hanging with the Elvi can get pretty confusing. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They can change theirs whenever they like.\'94 The Elvi all said in unity and then laughed heartily. This was not the first time this suggestion had been made, but each of them, in equal measure, held precious the name Elvis. The Elvi claimed they can tell each other apart, but Kleo found that quite difficult to swallow.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Sages arrived in The Quarter as conquering heroes returning from battle. Several hundred metres of the main thoroughfare was now gleaming and Elvi were lined either side ten deep, delighted and cheering, each desperate to touch the cloak of one of the prophets. A small lectern had been set up, just outside Parliament House (the old brothel), in case one of the Sages wished to delight the crowd with a few words of praise.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Defenders of the Dawkins, the cosmos is all that is, ever was or ever will be.\'94 Kleo bellowed out to the mass of mesmerized Elvi who cheered madly upon hearing the great sage\'92s wise words. \'93We are overjoyed by your welcome and look forward to spreading the word of science and reason with you all.\'94 Kleo look out upon the sea of faces, all glowing with love for The Dawkins. \'93Science and Reason pave the way towards the truth, but remember, there is no ultimate truth. Praise be to his name.\'94
